title: Genesis 16 – Hagar and Ishmael
description: A verse-by-verse study of Genesis 16: Sarai gives Hagar to Abram, the birth of Ishmael, and the allegory of the bondwoman and the freewoman in Galatians 4.
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-16-hagar-and-ishmael.html

# Genesis series pattern (Genesis 1-5). Slide text is the author's own sentences from the Genesis 16 study
# (posts 6915, 6916). Fixed: "Issac" -> "Isaac"; "Ismael" -> "Ishmael"; "They've always been" -> "There have always been".

=== Introduction
--- Genesis Chapter 16 [title]
overline: Young Adult Sunday School • Genesis Series
heading: Genesis 16: Hagar and Ishmael
sub: Impatient with God • The Bondwoman • The Children of Promise
refs: Genesis 16:1-16
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

=== Sarai’s plan
--- Sarai Gave Hagar
kicker: vv. 1–3
sub: After Abram Had Dwelt Ten Years in Canaan
scripture: Genesis 16:1-3 | mark: after Abram had dwelt ten years in the land of Canaan
p: The birth of Ishmael by the bondservant Hagar comes about when Abram is 86 and Sarai 76, the Bible says about 10 years after settling in Canaan, time well past God’s promise to Abram for an heir, as man reckons. [[Genesis 16:16]] [[Genesis 15:4]]

--- Her Mistress Was Despised
kicker: vv. 4–6
sub: Impatient with God, Lacking Faith
scripture: Genesis 16:4-6
p: Impatient with God, lacking faith, desperate for an heir, and wanting a child by any means, Sarai convinces Abram to sin. To have what is an illegitimate offspring in place of the promised son. Another older brother, who doesn’t receive the inheritance or God’s blessing. Like Cain or Esau. Or the Jews.

=== Hagar in the wilderness
--- The Angel of the {Lord} Found Her
kicker: vv. 7–10
sub: Return to Thy Mistress
scripture: Genesis 16:7-10

--- Thou Shalt Call His Name Ishmael
kicker: vv. 11–12
sub: He Will Be a Wild Man
scripture: Genesis 16:11-12 | mark: his hand will be against every man, and every man’s hand against him

--- Thou God Seest Me
kicker: vv. 13–16
sub: Hagar Bare Abram a Son
scripture: Genesis 16:13-16 | mark: Thou God seest me

=== The bondwoman and the freewoman
--- Which Things Are an Allegory
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 16:15
fig: Galatians 4:22-23 | Galatians 4:22-23
fig: Galatians 4:24-26 | Galatians 4:24-26

--- Which Things Are an Allegory, continued
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 16:15
fig: Galatians 4:28-29 | Galatians 4:28-29
fig: Galatians 4:30 | Galatians 4:30
callout: This theme, of the elder of the flesh being rejected for the son of the Spirit, of the promise, exists to teach us the way in which we who are sons of God in faith are the true heirs after Abraham, and those of the flesh who rejected Christ are like Ishmael. Cast out.

--- Cast Out the Bondwoman
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 21:9–12
sub: The Son of the Bondwoman Shall Not Be Heir
scripture: Genesis 21:10-12 | mark: Cast out this bondwoman and her son
p: In Genesis 21, in accordance with Sarah’s wishes and the {Lord}’s command, Abraham reluctantly banishes his firstborn, Ishmael, and the boy’s mother, the slave Hagar. Just as those under the law, using their own works to justify themselves before God, are cast out. Children of the bondwoman. But those who were conceived by faith, like Isaac was, the saved believers justified in Christ, receive the inheritance.

=== Works religion
--- All Works-Based False Religion
kicker: Application • Galatians 4
sub: Back Under Bondage
p: This extends not only to those Jews who developed the Talmudic Judaism that spun out of the Pharisaical line following the death and resurrection of Jesus, but to all works-based false religion. In Galatians, Paul writes warning against those Judaizers who seek to put the foolish Galatians back under bondage. There have always been those seeking to undermine the faith that calls upon the name of the {Lord} for salvation. From the fig leaves in the garden to Cain bringing his vegetables and fruit that he labored to grow. Right unto today, with Catholic sacrament and works, Buddhists and Hindus and Muslims. And of course Jews of every stripe. [[Galatians 5:1]] [[Genesis 3:7]] [[Genesis 4:3]]

--- Ishmael and Islam
kicker: A correlation • Genesis 16:12
sub: The Son of the Bondwoman
p: Now Ishmael is said to be the father of what would be Islam: that the son of the bondwoman’s promised seed were the Arabs and Mohammed. And their acceptance of Jesus as a prophet, but denying His sacrifice to instead trust in their own works, is a reflection of the sin of Sarah and Abraham with Hagar. It’s an interesting correlation, given us by revelation in God’s word. [[Genesis 17:20]]

--- Children of Promise
center: We, brethren, as Isaac was, are the children of promise. Not children of the bondwoman, but of the free. [[Galatians 4:28]] [[Galatians 4:31]]
